{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/881500-will-black-dog-publishing-s-return-on-the-20-years-anniversary","id":881500,"title":"Will Black Dog Publishing's return on the 20 Years Anniversary?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-05-03T22:10:05-07:00","id":881500,"title":"Will Black Dog Publishing's return on the 20 Years Anniversary?","content":"so..will the R rated books do a comeback for the &quot;20 Years of&quot; ?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Forum's Official's Joker and Trickster. Pardon my bad english, aint my first language (I Speak Spanish).<br /> ST: DtF, HtR, WtO, MtA<br /> Signature Chars: Crowley (hakalu), Joe The Nuwisha (WtA)<br /> Changelings: be afraid of the Technocracian High Five of Doom","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1754-crowley","name":"Crowley","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1754_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-03T22:17:13-07:00","id":881511,"title":"","content":"Black Dog stopped really being a thing during the Revised era as WW figured out it was kinda pointless. Plenty of the 20th books have touched on such topics without resurrecting the old imprint.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-03T22:32:33-07:00","id":881518,"title":"","content":"Black Dog was a blatant publicity stunt to appeal to vapid 90s edginess. I'd like it to stay buried.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-03T22:55:37-07:00","id":881536,"title":"","content":"Leave it as a Pentex subsidiary, strictly an in-universe thing that satirizes the real-world White Wolf. We don't need a real-world Black Dog imprint, and never did: the best of the Black Dog supplements could have been published under the White Wolf imprint, and the rest of them shouldn't have been published in the first place.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-04T07:09:56-07:00","id":881748,"title":"","content":"Dataweaver put it well. The good stuff was even better then a lot of main-line stuff, and showed a lot of research and investment in exploring even dark topics. The bad stuff was pure pulpy 90s edgyness for edgyness sake, and was just a way to drive controversy and sale with the branding.<br /> <br /> I'm all for dark messed up shit. It's what has made WW games intriguing. Just do it tasteful and don't make me go through Freak Legion or Eternal Hearts again.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-04T08:33:17-07:00","id":881824,"title":"","content":"Its gone the way of the G- word, pluss its not needed, The Novel Wyrm Wolf, has a Borderline Pornographic Love Scene and isnt labeled black dog.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-04T08:40:16-07:00","id":881832,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/881500-will-black-dog-publishing-s-return-on-the-20-years-anniversary?p=881536#post881536\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Leave it as a Pentex subsidiary, strictly an in-universe thing that satirizes the real-world White Wolf. We don't need a real-world Black Dog imprint, and never did: the best of the Black Dog supplements could have been published under the White Wolf imprint, and the rest of them shouldn't have been published in the first place.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sorry, but you are wrong. Your personal feelings about the value of the Black Dog books aside, we were most certainly unable to publish those books as WW at the time Black Dog was created and for some time after and expect store owners to simply stock them as our other books.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5-richt","name":"RichT","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5_2.jpeg","title":"Onyx Path Creative Director","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-04T08:45:46-07:00","id":881836,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/881500-will-black-dog-publishing-s-return-on-the-20-years-anniversary?p=881518#post881518\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Black Dog was a blatant publicity stunt to appeal to vapid 90s edginess. I'd like it to stay buried.</div> </div> </div> </div>Nope. Black Dog was created because the sales environment at the time was restricting the type of material we could publish. Some developers may have taken things too far, but others created books that we never could have published covering the mature topics we wanted to cover. Black Dog was a shield against censorship, and also protected store owners from lawsuits by outraged parents or local law enforcement. Stores were ruined by those things in the US at that time, and some store owners were naturally freaked out.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":10}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5-richt","name":"RichT","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5_2.jpeg","title":"Onyx Path Creative Director","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-04T10:02:00-07:00","id":881929,"title":"","content":"So rich, Will we ever see the return of a R-Rated book under the Black Dog Logo?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Forum's Official's Joker and Trickster. Pardon my bad english, aint my first language (I Speak Spanish).<br /> ST: DtF, HtR, WtO, MtA<br /> Signature Chars: Crowley (hakalu), Joe The Nuwisha (WtA)<br /> Changelings: be afraid of the Technocracian High Five of Doom","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1754-crowley","name":"Crowley","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1754_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-04T10:20:14-07:00","id":881947,"title":"","content":"There was the ExXxalted book. I suppose one of the benefits of selling online is not having to worry about the same things.<br /> <br /> The RedBubble site has a <a href=\"http://www.redbubble.com/people/theonyxpath/works/12655207-subsidiary-black-dog-game-factory?c=303221-werewolf-the-apocalypse\" target=\"_blank\">Black Dog Game Factory t-shirt</a>. The shirts are great. But I'd bet if Black Dog Publishing pops up much it would be under White Wolf, especially if they plan to sell in stores.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 05-04-2016, 01:27 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-04T11:19:33-07:00","id":882005,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Crowley</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/881500-will-black-dog-publishing-s-return-on-the-20-years-anniversary?p=881929#post881929\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So rich, Will we ever see the return of a R-Rated book under the Black Dog Logo?</div> </div> </div> </div>From my read, most of our WW-based books have what would have been questionable elements back in the day, so it would take a pretty special case to go that route. What was shocking then is on HBO now, so the whole marketplace seems less likely to be concerned.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5-richt","name":"RichT","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5_2.jpeg","title":"Onyx Path Creative Director","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-04T12:31:51-07:00","id":882090,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/881500-will-black-dog-publishing-s-return-on-the-20-years-anniversary?p=881518#post881518\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Black Dog was a blatant publicity stunt to appeal to vapid 90s edginess. I'd like it to stay buried.</div> </div> </div> </div>Black Dog was the label under which one of the most complex and truly mature (like psycho-emotionally mature) RPG books ever was published: <i>Charnel Houses of Europe</i>. Before you pan it all as a stunt, you should consider that there was some pretty quality material released under its banner.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Sig","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2319-captotter","name":"CaptOtter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2319_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"405"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-04T12:40:57-07:00","id":882099,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CaptOtter</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/881500-will-black-dog-publishing-s-return-on-the-20-years-anniversary?p=882090#post882090\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Black Dog was the label under which one of the most complex and truly mature (like psycho-emotionally mature) RPG books ever was published: <i>Charnel Houses of Europe</i>. Before you pan it all as a stunt, you should consider that there was some pretty quality material released under its banner.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, the vagina-face Tzimisce book, Dirty Secrets of the Black Hand, and Freak Legion are all such mature works of art.<br /> <br /> I've made my beef with Charnel Houses known elsewhere.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-04T15:17:41-07:00","id":882278,"title":"","content":"I'd definitely argue for <i>Montreal by Night</i> being a worthwhile use of the imprint. (Even if its writers did seem willfully ignorant of the importance of hockey in Canadian culture.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3505-matt-the-bruins-fan","name":"Matt the Bruins fan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3505_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-04T16:07:17-07:00","id":882319,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/881500-will-black-dog-publishing-s-return-on-the-20-years-anniversary?p=882099#post882099\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yes, the vagina-face Tzimisce book, Dirty Secrets of the Black Hand, and Freak Legion are all such mature works of art.<br /> <br /> I've made my beef with Charnel Houses known elsewhere.</div> </div> </div> </div>And of the 3 books you first mentioned, only the 3rd, schlocky as it was, was actually under the Black Dog seal.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-04T17:42:43-07:00","id":882382,"title":"","content":"<br /> I loved Black Dog, personally. While not everything released under the banner was good, the majority of it was. I enjoyed it and still go back and read some of the old Black Dog books on occasion. Rich is right, though. Modern day Onyx Path books generally put most of what could be found under Black Dog in current books. So I'm not sure if there's much need for them.<br /> <br /> However, it would be cool to see some easter eggs or something in future releases. Oh, and I'd LOVE a Black Dog mug from the Red Bubble store.<br /> <br /> Hint hint.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">&quot;Steel isn't strong, boy. Flesh is stronger.&quot;</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/95-fat-larry","name":"Fat Larry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar95_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1337"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-04T17:43:54-07:00","id":882384,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/881500-will-black-dog-publishing-s-return-on-the-20-years-anniversary?p=882099#post882099\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yes, the vagina-face Tzimisce book, Dirty Secrets of the Black Hand, and Freak Legion are all such mature works of art.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I don't think these were all Black Dog books. But I could be wrong. And I liked Freak Legion!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">&quot;Steel isn't strong, boy. Flesh is stronger.&quot;</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/95-fat-larry","name":"Fat Larry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar95_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1337"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-04T18:50:53-07:00","id":882418,"title":"","content":"Like any imprint from any publisher, there were some good and some bad things. <i>Giovanni Chronicles</i>, <i>Cainite Heresy</i>, <i>Clanbook: Baali</i>, <i>Hunter Book: Wayward</i>, as well as <i>Dead Magic</i> and <i>Ascension's Right Hand</i> along with the aforementioned <i>CHoE</i> outweigh <i>Cb: Tzimisce</i> (which was decently-written and shed a lot of light on the Dragons), and <i>DSotBH</i> (and <i>FL</i> was gross but good - it was no <i>FaTaL</i>; people actually liked it and it was usable).<br /> <br /> Let's also not forget that Black Dog was the imprint that published the hilarious and satirical <i>Human \u00f6ccupied Landfill</i> and its companion <i>BUTTery wH\u00f6Lsomeness</i>, and should be reinstated solely for that.<br /> <br /> Cheers!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If you don't use an Oxford comma, I feel bad for you, son,<br /> 'Cuz I got ninety-nine problems, but clarity ain't one.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/408-nothing","name":"nothing","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar408_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"572"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-04T21:04:08-07:00","id":882514,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-family:courier new\">As thorough as <i>Possessed</i> is, it just doesn\u2019t have the same je ne sais quoi as <i>Freak Legion</i>. Also, vibro blades. </span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:8px\"><span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\">&lt;signature&gt; something witty &lt;/signature&gt;</span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/302-nazfool","name":"Nazfool","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar302_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"753"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-04T22:09:00-07:00","id":882552,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/302-nazfool\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar302_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"302\" data-vbnamecard=\"302\">Nazfool</a> I don't think <i>Possessed</i> fully transmitted the <u>horror</u> of being Fomori. I mean, yeah, &quot;cool&quot; (and I use that very loosely) powers, tech, and juvenile gross-out stuff, but once you stepped back and parsed it, it was pure body horror. More so than playing a Spectre, I feel - at least as a Spectre, you had your Psyche slapping you around every once in a while to try to pull you back from that edge, but being Fomori was just suffering until you die (and then <i>maybe</i> that's it).<br /> <br /> I don't know anybody that actually <i>played</i> Freak Legion, but I know a lot of Storytellers that actually <i>used</i> it.<br /> <br /> Cheers!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If you don't use an Oxford comma, I feel bad for you, son,<br /> 'Cuz I got ninety-nine problems, but clarity ain't one.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/408-nothing","name":"nothing","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar408_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"572"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-05T01:09:40-07:00","id":882659,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>RichT</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/881500-will-black-dog-publishing-s-return-on-the-20-years-anniversary?p=881836#post881836\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Nope. Black Dog was created because the sales environment at the time was restricting the type of material we could publish. Some developers may have taken things too far, but others created books that we never could have published covering the mature topics we wanted to cover. Black Dog was a shield against censorship, and also protected store owners from lawsuits by outraged parents or local law enforcement. Stores were ruined by those things in the US at that time, and some store owners were naturally freaked out.</div> </div> </div> </div>I find this issue quite interesting. My European sensibilities may be showing but I've found most of the Black Dog stuff not to be all that drastically offensive or problematic (compared to the main lines with religious zealot terrorists, ghouls abasing themselves for a fix that can only come from the PC's and necrophilic incestous itallans) beyond the fact that some authors were really big on shock value.<br /> <br /> Could you tell us more about the climate at the time, the mission statement for Black Dog and how the books were chosen and why it's content was so controversial in the US?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-05T04:55:51-07:00","id":882777,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-family:courier new\"><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nothing</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/881500-will-black-dog-publishing-s-return-on-the-20-years-anniversary?p=882552#post882552\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> \u2026but once you stepped back and parsed it, it was pure body horror.</div> </div> </div> </div>I\u2019m not disagreeing. In fact, that\u2019s what I found so appealing.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nothing</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/881500-will-black-dog-publishing-s-return-on-the-20-years-anniversary?p=882552#post882552\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't know anybody that actually <i>played</i> Freak Legion, but I know a lot of Storytellers that actually <i>used</i> it.</div> </div> </div> </div>IKR! Back in the day, no one wanted to play a one- or two-shot because of the \u201clive hard, die fast\u201d ethos. Players (the ones I knew anyway) wanted characters with some sort of longevity.<br /> <br /> Luckily, that was some time ago. This last Halloween I ran a two night game with my old group. It evolved (or devolved, depending on your perspective) into \u2013 what I would call \u2013 Classic Freak Legion. They were brief, gore-filled, splatterpunk sessions more reminiscent of Troma than Lionsgate.<br /> <br /> Sadly, none of the players took the Fetish mop\u2026<br /> </span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\"><span style=\"font-family:courier new\">Anyway, good times all around!</span> <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:8px\">[Except for that poor Glasswalker.]</span></span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:8px\"><span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\">&lt;signature&gt; something witty &lt;/signature&gt;</span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/302-nazfool","name":"Nazfool","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar302_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"753"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-05T05:06:14-07:00","id":882782,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asmodai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/881500-will-black-dog-publishing-s-return-on-the-20-years-anniversary?p=882659#post882659\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I find this issue quite interesting. My European sensibilities may be showing but I've found most of the Black Dog stuff not to be all that drastically offensive or problematic (compared to the main lines with religious zealot terrorists, ghouls abasing themselves for a fix that can only come from the PC's and necrophilic incestous itallans) beyond the fact that some authors were really big on shock value.<br /> <br /> Could you tell us more about the climate at the time, the mission statement for Black Dog and how the books were chosen and why it's content was so controversial in the US?</div> </div> </div> </div>The opening fiction of Clanbooks Baali was child rape. It was a good book (as was that opening story but I can understand the Black Dog label for it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3075-coridan","name":"Coridan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3075_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"528"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-05T05:09:29-07:00","id":882784,"title":"","content":"Yes, and would you argue that a graphic description of child rape has in any way improved the book or was critical in understanding how depraved they are? I know the same about the Giovanni, and their freakish tendencies of incest, necrophilia and children abuse, yet it's in a &quot;mainstream&quot; book. I know the samea bout the sevent generation as well. So what do you gain from the graphic story there other then cheap shock value?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-05T07:17:55-07:00","id":882843,"title":"","content":"I do believe the story added to the book. It was dark and twisted, but well written. Have you read it?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3075-coridan","name":"Coridan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3075_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"528"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-05T09:52:35-07:00","id":882941,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/302-nazfool\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar302_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"302\" data-vbnamecard=\"302\">Nazfool</a> I know an ST that had his players take a break from their regular Werewolf/Mage game and play a session of Freak Legion. He had them make characters, play a single game, then gave them lots of experience points and let them spend immediately - he then used those Fomori as antagonists in the <i>very next</i> usual game he ran. The players were <i>pissed</i>, because they made their Fomori too well, and almost got steamrolled by their own creations. They were also pretty impressed after they figured out the things they were fighting, they had just played. Probably the most creative use of<i> Freak Legion</i> I've heard about.<br /> <br /> Cheers!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If you don't use an Oxford comma, I feel bad for you, son,<br /> 'Cuz I got ninety-nine problems, but clarity ain't one.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/408-nothing","name":"nothing","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar408_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"572"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-05T14:35:48-07:00","id":883212,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Coridan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/881500-will-black-dog-publishing-s-return-on-the-20-years-anniversary?p=882843#post882843\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I do believe the story added to the book. It was dark and twisted, but well written. Have you read it?</div> </div> </div> </div>I have the book. And I still believe it's there for cheap shock value and to fulfill the Black Dog requirement of &quot;This Controversial to Publish&quot;.<br /> <br /> I'd love to hear more from Rich about it, as it's the kind of thing that fascinates me. Where do you put the line and what was it that was threatening them at the time.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-05T15:39:03-07:00","id":883260,"title":"","content":"Censorship in the US in the late 80s/early 90s is kind of impossible to explain, because it was a complete mess. There was little inherent logic to it; even in more &quot;regulated&quot; industries like the music business (see: the PMRC). Nobody wanted to be the next circus paraded in front of Congress and forced to hammer out some sort of weird self-regulation agreement to keep moral-panic-happy censorship movements off their backs. Slapping a label on your &quot;worst&quot; offenders - pretty much regardless of how you defined them - was the general compromise. If you had some way of saying, &quot;this is our most 'view discretion advised,'&quot; material, it generally shielded you (and your distributors) from moral-panic backlash (when a kid decides he's actually a vampire and uses that to justify killing people VtM is the first to blame; and yes that did happen). To a large extent, nobody really paid enough attention to where a given company set its lines as long as it was setting lines at all.<br /> <br /> Like I said, it was a complete mess.<br /> <br /> The fact that putting stickers that say, &quot;adult material,&quot; on your product is like say, &quot;Hey kids, buy me!&quot; was something the entertainment industry seemed just fine with as a whole, and completely lost on the, &quot;don't sell stuff to our kids we don't like,&quot; movements.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-06T04:23:14-07:00","id":883642,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/881500-will-black-dog-publishing-s-return-on-the-20-years-anniversary?p=882099#post882099\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yes, the vagina-face Tzimisce book, Dirty Secrets of the Black Hand, and Freak Legion are all such mature works of art.<br /> <br /> I've made my beef with Charnel Houses known elsewhere.</div> </div> </div> </div>Freak Legion, other than some questionable and truly hentai-worthy fomori powers, was awesome. Not necessarily mature, but worthy of publication all the same. Same with Human Occupied Landfill - tacky, in extremely poor taste, and nonetheless a solid product that deserved to be put into the world.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5307-loomer","name":"loomer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5307_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"661"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-06T05:27:58-07:00","id":883661,"title":"","content":"Yes, but why couldn't you publish HoL outside of Black Dog? It's a comedy product and the worst of its excesses are nothing compared to the casual horrors of Pentex, the Giovanni or the Nephandi.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-06T06:26:58-07:00","id":883688,"title":"","content":"I don't know if you could get away with doing so back in 1994. I mean, it was the first thing BDGF ever published, and as Rich said, the reality at the time was that a lot of RPG content was already being seen as 'too far', let alone something like HoL.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5307-loomer","name":"loomer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5307_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"661"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-06T06:39:30-07:00","id":883698,"title":"","content":"But my point is that if HoL is too much, how are the Tzimisce, the Giovanni and the Book of the Wyrm not too much? Where is this line and who defines it?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-06T06:51:14-07:00","id":883709,"title":"","content":"Market forces, and the issue is it isn't a clear line most of the time. Take Jacobellis v Ohio's famous definition of obscenity (though it was not obscenity per se in that case but specifically pornography; it has however been broadly applied since) given by Justice Stewart: &quot;I know it when I see it.&quot;<br /> <br /> So really, the line isn't defined in the sense we'd hope for. It's a continuum depending on exactly who's categorizing it, where, and for what purpose.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5307-loomer","name":"loomer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5307_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"661"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-06T07:05:53-07:00","id":883720,"title":"","content":"I might be giving voice to terrible heresy, but I honestly prefer Freak Legions over Possessed. I legitimately enjoy Freak Legion's splatter-punk sludge metal feel, whereas Possessed always seemed kind of sterile. Overall the additional rules density of Possessed is a plus, but the introduction of Autonomy shot the whole enterprise in the foot by punishing anyone who wanted to treat Fomori as anything other than disposable mutant mooks that could be conveniently torn apart with no moral ramifications. Freak Legions, whatever its other faults, presents Fomori as people with a problem. Deeply flawed people trapped in a cycle of debasement they themselves often initiated, but people nonetheless. Possessed is a textbook, Freak Legions is a game supplement.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2507-caitiff-primogen","name":"Caitiff Primogen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2507_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-06T07:12:59-07:00","id":883729,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Caitiff Primogen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/881500-will-black-dog-publishing-s-return-on-the-20-years-anniversary?p=883720#post883720\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I might be giving voice to terrible heresy, but I honestly prefer Freak Legions over Possessed. I legitimately enjoy Freak Legion's splatter-punk sludge metal feel, whereas Possessed always seemed kind of sterile.</div> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"font-family:courier new\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Heresy? This is preaching to the choir. </span></span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:8px\"><span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\">&lt;signature&gt; something witty &lt;/signature&gt;</span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/302-nazfool","name":"Nazfool","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar302_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"753"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-06T09:14:03-07:00","id":883834,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nazfool</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/881500-will-black-dog-publishing-s-return-on-the-20-years-anniversary?p=883729#post883729\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"font-family:courier new\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Heresy? This is preaching to the choir. </span></span></div> </div> </div> </div>Not to mention Freak Legion had probably no small bit of influence in some of the terminology and concepts of Aberrant - damn, my first impression of the game was that the Novas were redressed Fomori until i read enough to be sure it was a completely different setting with no connection to the World of Darkness. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-06T11:02:44-07:00","id":883904,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1182_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1182\" data-vbnamecard=\"1182\">Asmodai</a> As others have mentioned, it takes a bit of American historical context to really understand the situation. There has always been a strain of &quot;American Puritanism,&quot; and in the 90's it was focused on &quot;entertainments&quot; - movies, music, and video games (like it almost always is). In the 80's, Tipper Gore and her group had successfully browbeaten the music industry into &quot;voluntarily&quot; placing 'Parental Advisory' labels on &quot;objectionable&quot; music (the standards used were laughable and arbitrary - any references to smoking, drinking, drugs, and swearing warranted a sticker, but songs about beating women, as long as they didn't contain any of those previous mentions, were perfectly fine. There wasn't so much as a &quot;committee&quot; as a checklist). In the 90's, several &quot;Parent Advocacy&quot; and interest groups began rumbling and eyeing the entertainment industry again, most especially the burgeoning video game companies. In a move to head off the possible storm of controversy (and censorship, and court, and government regulation), several sectors began a process of &quot;self-regulation&quot; - it's why the ESRB was created. Other, smaller sectors - like role-playing games - followed suit. White Wolf created the Black Dog imprint to publish things that were deemed &quot;too mature&quot; for the main line - things that may have lead to retailers returning and discontinuing their White Wolf orders (as a special side note, <i>Clanbook: Tzimisce</i> was originally published in a 'censored' format by White Wolf, since it predated the creation of Black Dog, and was later republished uncensored under the Black Dog label). As for <i>H\u00f6L</i>, amazing as it was, White Wolf did not want it immediately associated with them and confused with the World of Darkness (as the two were basically synonymous at the time).<br /> <br /> As for &quot;where is this line and who defines it,&quot; well... it's a self-imposed measure. It really depends on the sociopolitical landscape and the personal feelings of whomever is in charge of publishing at the time. So there's no hard metric.<br /> <br /> Cheers!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If you don't use an Oxford comma, I feel bad for you, son,<br /> 'Cuz I got ninety-nine problems, but clarity ain't one.","edited":{"userid":408,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/408-nothing","user":"nothing","date":". 05-06-2016, 02:49 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/408-nothing","name":"nothing","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar408_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"572"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-06T11:19:46-07:00","id":883915,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-family:courier new\">I don't think the original <i>Clanbook: Tzimisce</i> was ever a Black Dog print. <i>Montreal by Night</i> and <i>Clanbook: Baali</i>, yes. <i>Clanbook: Dentata</i>, no.</span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:8px\"><span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\">&lt;signature&gt; something witty &lt;/signature&gt;</span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/302-nazfool","name":"Nazfool","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar302_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"753"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-06T11:47:31-07:00","id":883940,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/302-nazfool\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar302_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"302\" data-vbnamecard=\"302\">Nazfool</a> You're right - I'm mis-remembering. <i>Cb:T</i> was never a Black Dog book, and it wasn't &quot;published&quot; in un/censored versions. Depending on the retailer (or maybe the warehouse? Or shipper?), it was either brown-bagged, black poly-bagged, or just had a black bar over most of the rear illo. I think the confusion comes from a mention somewhere that <i>Cb:T</i> <u>should</u> have been a Black Dog book in retrospect.<br /> <br /> Cheers!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If you don't use an Oxford comma, I feel bad for you, son,<br /> 'Cuz I got ninety-nine problems, but clarity ain't one.","edited":{"userid":408,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/408-nothing","user":"nothing","date":". 05-06-2016, 02:50 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/408-nothing","name":"nothing","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar408_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"572"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-06T13:52:38-07:00","id":884044,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Caitiff Primogen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/881500-will-black-dog-publishing-s-return-on-the-20-years-anniversary?p=883720#post883720\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I might be giving voice to terrible heresy, but I honestly prefer Freak Legions over Possessed. I legitimately enjoy Freak Legion's splatter-punk sludge metal feel, whereas Possessed always seemed kind of sterile. Overall the additional rules density of Possessed is a plus, but the introduction of Autonomy shot the whole enterprise in the foot by punishing anyone who wanted to treat Fomori as anything other than disposable mutant mooks that could be conveniently torn apart with no moral ramifications. Freak Legions, whatever its other faults, presents Fomori as people with a problem. Deeply flawed people trapped in a cycle of debasement they themselves often initiated, but people nonetheless. Possessed is a textbook, Freak Legions is a game supplement.</div> </div> </div> </div>Possessed had to cover an awful lot of additional material, including drones. It could have been a bit longer, in retrospect. Also, Autonomy needed to not cap Willpower, but I'm not getting how it cements fomori as cannon fodder mutants, since you have to make the human character first, and the first hit of powers (five points worth, formerly paid for by the rather clunky Breed Notoriety Taint that wasn't really a Taint at all) was free.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-06T22:08:02-07:00","id":884378,"title":"","content":"Now that i think about it, im surprised that Slashers didnt came out under Black Dog.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Forum's Official's Joker and Trickster. Pardon my bad english, aint my first language (I Speak Spanish).<br /> ST: DtF, HtR, WtO, MtA<br /> Signature Chars: Crowley (hakalu), Joe The Nuwisha (WtA)<br /> Changelings: be afraid of the Technocracian High Five of Doom","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1754-crowley","name":"Crowley","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1754_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-06T22:09:54-07:00","id":884381,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>RichT</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/881500-will-black-dog-publishing-s-return-on-the-20-years-anniversary?p=882005#post882005\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> From my read, most of our WW-based books have what would have been questionable elements back in the day, so it would take a pretty special case to go that route. What was shocking then is on HBO now, so the whole marketplace seems less likely to be concerned.</div> </div> </div> </div>No chances for it to come back as a little &quot;Homage&quot; to the old players? i mean, if for example Slashers were to be revised, no chances for it to be Printed under Black Dog or any mention inside the credits?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Forum's Official's Joker and Trickster. Pardon my bad english, aint my first language (I Speak Spanish).<br /> ST: DtF, HtR, WtO, MtA<br /> Signature Chars: Crowley (hakalu), Joe The Nuwisha (WtA)<br /> Changelings: be afraid of the Technocracian High Five of Doom","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1754-crowley","name":"Crowley","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1754_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-07T00:04:45-07:00","id":884425,"title":"","content":"It's the new WW's call now anyway, since they own the BDG imprint, not Onyx Path.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-07T06:22:04-07:00","id":884577,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-family:courier new\">Given that Black Dog is<br /> A) owned by White Wolf (i.e., Paradox) and<br /> B) It\u2019d be unnecessary nowadays<br /> I\u2019m not seeing a reason or need to have a Black Dog label.<br /> <br /> For the sake of conversation, however, here are snippets from inane ramblings that were part of this post\u2019s first draft. I removed all the daft bits. So quite a bit.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\">Nazfoolishness:<br /> It might be interesting to see the ethos of Black Dog turned into a game, just nothing involving the current systems or setting. Right now I\u2019m imagining a game/setting that coalesce all the sociopolitical fears and paranoids of the 1980s and 1990s (at least in the US) into a cohesive parody. I\u2019m thinking of a <i>HoL</i>\u2013esque layout with an artistic vibe that combines old <i>Tales from the Crypt</i>, <i>Metalocaplyse</i>, and <i>Korgoth of Barbaria</i>.*</span><br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:10px\">*and <i>Starbarians</i> on YouTube.</span></span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:8px\"><span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\">&lt;signature&gt; something witty &lt;/signature&gt;</span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/302-nazfool","name":"Nazfool","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar302_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"753"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-07T18:02:58-07:00","id":885048,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Crowley</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/881500-will-black-dog-publishing-s-return-on-the-20-years-anniversary?p=884381#post884381\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> No chances for it to come back as a little &amp;quot;Homage&amp;quot; to the old players? i mean, if for example Slashers were to be revised, no chances for it to be Printed under Black Dog or any mention inside the credits?</div> </div> </div> </div>Why would we do that? Just to tickle the old fancies?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5-richt","name":"RichT","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5_2.jpeg","title":"Onyx Path Creative Director","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-07T18:07:40-07:00","id":885054,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>RichT</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/881500-will-black-dog-publishing-s-return-on-the-20-years-anniversary?p=885048#post885048\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why would we do that? Just to tickle the old fancies?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Maybe don't publish under it as a separate label, but if there's a book that goes a bit darker than normal fare, throw the logo on for funsies.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3075-coridan","name":"Coridan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3075_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"528"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-07T18:20:04-07:00","id":885063,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asmodai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/881500-will-black-dog-publishing-s-return-on-the-20-years-anniversary?p=883698#post883698\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But my point is that if HoL is too much, how are the Tzimisce, the Giovanni and the Book of the Wyrm not too much? Where is this line and who defines it?</div> </div> </div> </div>You seem to be desperate to sustain some sort of thesis. Life, and publishing, doesn't fall into neat slots that justify a conveniently over-arching rationale. We created Black Dog because WW wanted to create projects with a &quot;shield&quot; that gave us distance from the censorship and paranoia of the time period we created it in. The angry claims that WW was filled with &quot;faggots and satanists&quot; and the understandable fears by store owners that they would be sued unto ruin if they put something on the general shelves that &quot;my Bobby&quot; shouldn't see. Tzimisce was one of the pre-Black Dog projects that led to Black Dog, and HOL with a fuck averaging every other paragraph was the first example of something WW couldn't get into our regular stores but that we felt deserved to be out there where folks could decide on their own whether it was offensive, or fun and offensive. Past that, our very diverse crew of creators put forth a wide variety of projects. Some you personally might say did not &quot;deserve&quot; the BD brand, but frankly, deserved was never the point. <br /> <br /> It wasn't a concerted effort to produce products for the Black Dog &quot;line&quot;, it was a shield so folks could create projects unrestricted by the needs of stores and distributors.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5-richt","name":"RichT","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5_2.jpeg","title":"Onyx Path Creative Director","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-07T20:55:51-07:00","id":885136,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>RichT</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/881500-will-black-dog-publishing-s-return-on-the-20-years-anniversary?p=885048#post885048\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why would we do that? Just to tickle the old fancies?</div> </div> </div> </div>not to be published under any other label, but mainly as a Shoutout to the players who grew up with those R label books?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Forum's Official's Joker and Trickster. Pardon my bad english, aint my first language (I Speak Spanish).<br /> ST: DtF, HtR, WtO, MtA<br /> Signature Chars: Crowley (hakalu), Joe The Nuwisha (WtA)<br /> Changelings: be afraid of the Technocracian High Five of Doom","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1754-crowley","name":"Crowley","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1754_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-08T10:21:10-07:00","id":885468,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>RichT</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/881500-will-black-dog-publishing-s-return-on-the-20-years-anniversary?p=885063#post885063\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You seem to be desperate to sustain some sort of thesis. Life, and publishing, doesn't fall into neat slots that justify a conveniently over-arching rationale. We created Black Dog because WW wanted to create projects with a &quot;shield&quot; that gave us distance from the censorship and paranoia of the time period we created it in. The angry claims that WW was filled with &quot;faggots and satanists&quot; and the understandable fears by store owners that they would be sued unto ruin if they put something on the general shelves that &quot;my Bobby&quot; shouldn't see. Tzimisce was one of the pre-Black Dog projects that led to Black Dog, and HOL with a fuck averaging every other paragraph was the first example of something WW couldn't get into our regular stores but that we felt deserved to be out there where folks could decide on their own whether it was offensive, or fun and offensive. Past that, our very diverse crew of creators put forth a wide variety of projects. Some you personally might say did not &quot;deserve&quot; the BD brand, but frankly, deserved was never the point.<br /> <br /> It wasn't a concerted effort to produce products for the Black Dog &quot;line&quot;, it was a shield so folks could create projects unrestricted by the needs of stores and distributors.</div> </div> </div> </div>Or, more precisely, create projects that met the needs of the stores and distributors and allowed the greater latitude for the creator to more fully realize the product?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-08T19:28:59-07:00","id":885889,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/881500-will-black-dog-publishing-s-return-on-the-20-years-anniversary?p=884044#post884044\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Possessed had to cover an awful lot of additional material, including drones. It could have been a bit longer, in retrospect. Also, Autonomy needed to not cap Willpower, but I'm not getting how it cements fomori as cannon fodder mutants, since you have to make the human character first, and the first hit of powers (five points worth, formerly paid for by the rather clunky Breed Notoriety Taint that wasn't really a Taint at all) was free.</div> </div> </div> </div>YMMV, I've just encountered a number of Werewolf players who have argued that Fomori are not human because the bane has consumed their souls and since they are not human there's no ethical questions to be asked by killing them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2507-caitiff-primogen","name":"Caitiff Primogen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2507_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-08T20:33:40-07:00","id":885930,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Caitiff Primogen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/881500-will-black-dog-publishing-s-return-on-the-20-years-anniversary?p=885889#post885889\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">YMMV, I've just encountered a number of Werewolf players who have argued that Fomori are not human because the bane has consumed their souls and since they are not human there's no ethical questions to be asked by killing them.</div> </div> </div> </div>Did they specifically say it was because of Autonomy? Because it's only at Autonomy 0 that anything like that actually happens.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-08T21:59:49-07:00","id":885960,"title":"","content":"Autonomy was generally a central part of their argument.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2507-caitiff-primogen","name":"Caitiff Primogen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2507_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-09T03:07:11-07:00","id":886067,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>RichT</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/881500-will-black-dog-publishing-s-return-on-the-20-years-anniversary?p=885063#post885063\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You seem to be desperate to sustain some sort of thesis. Life, and publishing, doesn't fall into neat slots that justify a conveniently over-arching rationale. We created Black Dog because WW wanted to create projects with a &quot;shield&quot; that gave us distance from the censorship and paranoia of the time period we created it in. The angry claims that WW was filled with &quot;faggots and satanists&quot; and the understandable fears by store owners that they would be sued unto ruin if they put something on the general shelves that &quot;my Bobby&quot; shouldn't see. Tzimisce was one of the pre-Black Dog projects that led to Black Dog, and HOL with a fuck averaging every other paragraph was the first example of something WW couldn't get into our regular stores but that we felt deserved to be out there where folks could decide on their own whether it was offensive, or fun and offensive. Past that, our very diverse crew of creators put forth a wide variety of projects. Some you personally might say did not &quot;deserve&quot; the BD brand, but frankly, deserved was never the point.<br /> <br /> It wasn't a concerted effort to produce products for the Black Dog &quot;line&quot;, it was a shield so folks could create projects unrestricted by the needs of stores and distributors.</div> </div> </div> </div>I get that, and I'm really not trying to say you guys did anything bad. I've grown up with White Wolf's books and they were something truly special for me in what I consider my formative years. However, when you say that Black Dog was there to protect you, I ask about it because I'm a bit confused considering the kind of material that is normal in WW. I cannot presume to understand the publishing or moral stances of 90s America, because at the time you guys made Black Dog, bombs were still falling here<br /> <br /> So, I'm asking you as someone who has a unique perspective and experience here and who understands what led to this, what was the actual point and reasoning for making a certain book Black Dog. Was it just to be a lightning rod? Did anyone actually consider Black Dog a separate entity at the time?<br /> <br /> I mean... the main lines are loaded with messed up stuff and seriously weird ideas:<ul><li>rape of both physical and mental nature,</li> <li>bizzare morale codes that would cause serious mayhem if they were actually read by people responsible for the moral outrage</li> <li>sex as in the act and as in implication and innuendo, not to mention a lot of non-vanilla sex activities</li> <li>abuse of children (and people in general)</li> <li>casual murder up to and including sacrificing people for life/magic/power</li> <li>Body Horror</li> </ul><br /> I'm sure I've forgotten something, but there was a reason why you had the label of &quot;Games for mature minds&quot;. Compared to the weight and weirdness of your normal material, what actually made the Black Dog games so much different? A lot of the books that were published under Black Dog were either not especially worse then the normal content. And while I get that great books like say Shoah or Infernalism would have raised a fuss... the others just felt like more of the same with added edginess - Destiny's Price, Baali and Freak Legion come out as puerile. And considering the expletives and general freakyness of the normal WoD, HoL just feels like sophomoric silliness, barely worse then 80s John Belushi.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-09T06:39:38-07:00","id":886166,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Caitiff Primogen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/881500-will-black-dog-publishing-s-return-on-the-20-years-anniversary?p=885960#post885960\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Autonomy was generally a central part of their argument.</div> </div> </div> </div>But AUTONOMY DOES NOT WORK THAT WAY! They'd have a better time trying to argue something about how difficult it is to get the bane out and not kill the fomor, and even that is a question of technical difficulty and less than perfectly available Gifts making for a tragic inability to help rather than &quot;they're already gone beyond all help&quot;.<br /> <br /> With Autonomy, though, you can actually make degeneration go backward and accept Taints in order to get back more control. Unfortunately, this leads to a situation where the most outwardly monstrous fomori are the ones in greater control of themselves, while those that look normal are closer to being lost to the bane's whims, but you do get to tell the bane to sit down and shut up.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":23,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","user":"Saur Ops Specialist","date":". 05-09-2016, 09:41 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-09T11:52:56-07:00","id":886515,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asmodai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/881500-will-black-dog-publishing-s-return-on-the-20-years-anniversary?p=886067#post886067\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I mean... the main lines are loaded with messed up stuff and seriously weird ideas:<ul><li>rape of both physical and mental nature,</li> <li>bizzare morale codes that would cause serious mayhem if they were actually read by people responsible for the moral outrage</li> <li>sex as in the act and as in implication and innuendo, not to mention a lot of non-vanilla sex activities</li> <li>abuse of children (and people in general)</li> <li>casual murder up to and including sacrificing people for life/magic/power</li> <li>Body Horror</li> </ul><br /> .</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Coincidentally, this type of subject matter is what drew me to the World of Darkness in the first place. I love playing games with a modern setting and I love horror. When White Wolf meshed the two together(&quot;like the real world but DARKER&quot;), I was in heaven. <br /> <br /> Still am, really. 20 years later, and the cWoD is still my favorite rpg of all time. ChroD is fantastic, too. <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">&quot;Steel isn't strong, boy. Flesh is stronger.&quot;</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/95-fat-larry","name":"Fat Larry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar95_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1337"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-09T17:31:44-07:00","id":886785,"title":"","content":"Asmodai, it's more likely that in reality they could have gotten away with publishing the Black Dog stuff under the WW banner, which is why none of those other books really created much of an issue for them. Either they were too small (early 90s) or the Satanism scare had already waned (for example, Demon the Fallen was a book line lol). It was more caution that created the Black Dog label both on their part as publisher and for the gaming stores that would carry these books, rather than any real threat from parents rights groups.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3075-coridan","name":"Coridan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3075_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"528"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-10T08:01:59-07:00","id":887168,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Coridan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/881500-will-black-dog-publishing-s-return-on-the-20-years-anniversary?p=886785#post886785\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Asmodai, it's more likely that in reality they could have gotten away with publishing the Black Dog stuff under the WW banner, which is why none of those other books really created much of an issue for them. Either they were too small (early 90s) or the Satanism scare had already waned (for example, Demon the Fallen was a book line lol). It was more caution that created the Black Dog label both on their part as publisher and for the gaming stores that would carry these books, rather than any real threat from parents rights groups.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not really. Parent's groups, church groups, etc. were still there and were still making lots of waves. Satanism scare or no. Children vis-a-vis &quot;obscenity&quot; or &quot;these things make our kids go crazy/turn violent/whatever is a recurrent issue. The particular target varies with each crest of the wave - horror movies, heavy metal music, video games, RPGs, though you get some of the same things caught up in later waves. In the late '80's things were pretty bad for RPGs. The D&amp;D response was to try to take out all the demons and devils by the expedient of just renaming them. That was supposed to clear up who the bad guys were, make them less threatening to religious people, stop them from being used as patrons by those who wanted to go for that sort of play, etc. The &quot;wussification&quot; of D&amp;D at that point was probably one of the (many) factors that lead to a desire for &quot;darker&quot; games that gave us, no wonder at the name, a World of Darkness. Then the WoD gets it's own backlash in the mid-90s at the crest of another wave and we get Black Dog....<br /> <br /> It's just a matter of the ebb and flow of social issues and their effects on marketing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-10T10:15:18-07:00","id":887272,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asmodai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/881500-will-black-dog-publishing-s-return-on-the-20-years-anniversary?p=886067#post886067\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And considering the expletives and general freakyness of the normal WoD, HoL just feels like sophomoric silliness, barely worse then 80s John Belushi.</div> </div> </div> </div><i>H\u00f6L</i> <u>was</u> &quot;sophomoric silliness,&quot; because <i>H\u00f6L</i> was a <u>satire</u> of 90's &quot;edgy&quot; and &quot;grimdark&quot; games - notably<i> Warhammer 40K </i>and the World of Darkness; there's even specific reference to <i>Vampire</i>. <i>H\u00f6L</i> was a mockery, laughing at the things that supposedly made other games &quot;mature,&quot; and &quot;adult.&quot; One cannot examine <i>H\u00f6L</i> out of context - it was the <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dada\" target=\"_blank\">Dadaist</a> response to role-playing games at the time, a critique on the state of the industry and art.<br /> <br /> Now, I wasn't there<sup>1</sup>, but I'm pretty sure there were myriad reasons leading to publish <i>H\u00f6L</i> under the Black Dog banner; things like maybe &quot;One shouldn't publish a satire mocking one's cash cow<sup>2</sup> <b><i><u>alongside</u></i></b> said cash cow;&quot; and <i>H\u00f6L</i> being singularly excessive in striving to (comically) offend. It wasn't that <i>H\u00f6L</i> said &quot;fuck&quot; a few times, it was the fact that <i>H\u00f6L</i> said &quot;fuck&quot; <u>every time it could</u> (and a few it couldn't).<br /> <br /> Cheers!<br /> <br /> <sup>1 Or was I? No, no, I wasn't.<br /> 2 And thus, also mocking those players that conflate personal identity with favorite product.</sup><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If you don't use an Oxford comma, I feel bad for you, son,<br /> 'Cuz I got ninety-nine problems, but clarity ain't one.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/408-nothing","name":"nothing","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar408_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"572"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-11T01:21:35-07:00","id":887980,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5-richt\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar5_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"5\" data-vbnamecard=\"5\">RichT</a> Thanks for making that Monday Meeting post. I would have thought something like that would make good blog material. I always thought there was actual pressure on White Wolf as a company rather then the retailers. I'm assuming since there wasn't direct pressure on the company, most of the stuff would actually fly under the radar as it was hidden deep inside a book, and only the stuff that would on a casual look cause offense was branded Black Dog?<br /> <br /> I may suffer from a problem where I assume that the actual content would have been inspected (and oh boy would it have given fuel to the moral guardians), but they aren't really able to scratch beyond the surface...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-11T01:46:23-07:00","id":887988,"title":"","content":"In all honesty I ran afoul of parental intervention in my games back in the early days of WW. Which at one point included a sit down with my church's pastor concerning the nature of Garou spirituality and Christian ethos. Now in all honesty it wasn't a terrible thing nor did I care I have always had an open door policy for my games in that any parent was welcome to sit in on the game. But what set this particular Mom off was a news report involving a local comic/game store and the Werewolf the Apocalypse game ran in store that dared to outdraw a local church's youth group. The church boycotted and protested outside for several days and forced the store to stop offering gaming on site. And this happened before Black Dog was a thing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/293-lncbill","name":"lncbill","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar293_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-11T06:00:01-07:00","id":888092,"title":"","content":"Heck, both my parents played D&amp;D and suffered through all the satanic panic malarkey in the 80's and even <i>they</i> looked askance at me when I started playing White Wolf. It was a weird time.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2507-caitiff-primogen","name":"Caitiff Primogen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2507_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-12T08:26:24-07:00","id":889133,"title":"","content":"My grandfather, whom I loved deeply, was a devout Catholic and took me aside to warn me of the dangers of RPG and witchcraft. This was in the UK. I was playing SR and WFRPG and he'd seen the books, God knows what he'd have said if he ever came across WW (which I started playing soon after that talk).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11613-jozanna","name":"Jozanna","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-12T08:33:16-07:00","id":889139,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nothing</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/881500-will-black-dog-publishing-s-return-on-the-20-years-anniversary?p=887272#post887272\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <i>H\u00f6L</i> <u>was</u> &quot;sophomoric silliness,&quot; because <i>H\u00f6L</i> was a <u>satire</u> of 90's &quot;edgy&quot; and &quot;grimdark&quot; games - notably<i> Warhammer 40K </i>and the World of Darkness; there's even specific reference to <i>Vampire</i>. <i>H\u00f6L</i> was a mockery, laughing at the things that supposedly made other games &quot;mature,&quot; and &quot;adult.&quot; One cannot examine <i>H\u00f6L</i> out of context - it was the <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dada\" target=\"_blank\">Dadaist</a> response to role-playing games at the time, a critique on the state of the industry and art.</div> </div> </div> </div>This.<br /> <br /> HoL was made at a time when Cyberpunk's GM book was literally called &quot;Listen up, you primitive screwheads!!!&quot; It was a glorious time to be alive, and HoL parodied the hell out of the industry at the time.<br /> <br /> As to shrinkwrapping - my flgs at the time shrik-wrapped <i>everything</i>, which was extremely irritating. And Clanbook Tzimiscie was shrink-wrapped in a black bag.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Dave Brookshaw</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14-dave-brookshaw","name":"Dave Brookshaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2081"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-03T09:18:13-07:00","id":925375,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asmodai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/881500-will-black-dog-publishing-s-return-on-the-20-years-anniversary?p=882659#post882659\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I find this issue quite interesting. My European sensibilities may be showing but I've found most of the Black Dog stuff not to be all that drastically offensive or problematic (compared to the main lines with religious zealot terrorists, ghouls abasing themselves for a fix that can only come from the PC's and necrophilic incestous itallans) beyond the fact that some authors were really big on shock value.<br /> <br /> Could you tell us more about the climate at the time, the mission statement for Black Dog and how the books were chosen and why it's content was so controversial in the US?</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't know what it was like in RPGs, I hadn't gotten into the hobby yet, but comic shop owners had more than a few incidents.<br /> <br /> I remember two distinctly, both in Texas. Shop owners were arrested and charged with Public Obscenity over the cover of an issue of Gen 13 that featured half of a bare female ass (It was Fairchild and she was wearing a thong) and the Neil Gaiman penned HIV awareness pamplet &quot;Death Talks About Life&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/nbylxup\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/n18segp\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0v25ewp\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/n77xu8p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1667-novagain","name":"Novagain","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"92"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-03T09:34:04-07:00","id":925382,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Novagain</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/881500-will-black-dog-publishing-s-return-on-the-20-years-anniversary?p=925375#post925375\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">...and the Neil Gaiman penned HIV awareness pamplet &quot;Death Talks About Life&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"font-family:courier new\">I still have a copy of that! It taught me how to put a condom on! Which makes me sound really pathetic when I say it out loud. . . <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:8px\"><span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\">&lt;signature&gt; something witty &lt;/signature&gt;</span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/302-nazfool","name":"Nazfool","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar302_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"753"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-03T11:18:48-07:00","id":925422,"title":"","content":"Some of the Black Dog books were my favorite books in role-playing. Period. I would love to see a return of the label in some form, if possible. Maybe an over-sized hardcover of sorts with new material?<br /> <br /> I purchased the Black Dog Gaming shirt from the OP Red Bubble store. Probably my favorite shirt I own. : )","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00FF00\"><b>Hail Hydra. </b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12047-firstteam80","name":"FirstTeam80","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12047_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-03T11:36:19-07:00","id":925429,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nazfool</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/881500-will-black-dog-publishing-s-return-on-the-20-years-anniversary?p=925382#post925382\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"font-family:courier new\">I still have a copy of that! It taught me how to put a condom on! Which makes me sound really pathetic when I say it out loud. . . <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></span></div> </div> </div> </div>Hey, that's a completely necessary life skill that American society is terrible about communicating and educating today, let alone twenty years ago. If that's how you learned then the book did its job. Kudos.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2507-caitiff-primogen","name":"Caitiff Primogen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2507_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-03T12:31:25-07:00","id":925458,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nazfool</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/881500-will-black-dog-publishing-s-return-on-the-20-years-anniversary?p=925382#post925382\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"font-family:courier new\">I still have a copy of that! It taught me how to put a condom on! Which makes me sound really pathetic when I say it out loud. . . <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></span></div> </div> </div> </div>i got a copy as well!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Forum's Official's Joker and Trickster. Pardon my bad english, aint my first language (I Speak Spanish).<br /> ST: DtF, HtR, WtO, MtA<br /> Signature Chars: Crowley (hakalu), Joe The Nuwisha (WtA)<br /> Changelings: be afraid of the Technocracian High Five of Doom","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1754-crowley","name":"Crowley","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1754_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-03T14:54:43-07:00","id":925508,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ajax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/881500-will-black-dog-publishing-s-return-on-the-20-years-anniversary?p=887168#post887168\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not really. Parent's groups, church groups, etc. were still there and were still making lots of waves. Satanism scare or no. Children vis-a-vis &quot;obscenity&quot; or &quot;these things make our kids go crazy/turn violent/whatever is a recurrent issue. The particular target varies with each crest of the wave - horror movies, heavy metal music, video games, RPGs, though you get some of the same things caught up in later waves. In the late '80's things were pretty bad for RPGs. The D&amp;D response was to try to take out all the demons and devils by the expedient of just renaming them. That was supposed to clear up who the bad guys were, make them less threatening to religious people, stop them from being used as patrons by those who wanted to go for that sort of play, etc. The &quot;wussification&quot; of D&amp;D at that point was probably one of the (many) factors that lead to a desire for &quot;darker&quot; games that gave us, no wonder at the name, a World of Darkness. Then the WoD gets it's own backlash in the mid-90s at the crest of another wave and we get Black Dog....<br /> <br /> It's just a matter of the ebb and flow of social issues and their effects on marketing.</div> </div> </div> </div>Was there ever a controversy surrounding WW of the same or similar size that D&amp;D? I heard the D&amp;D one but not one particularly public of WW. Im however not american i honestly dont know? As side note, do they a mazes &amp; monster-like movie with Tom hanks? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/881500-will-black-dog-publishing-s-return-on-the-20-years-anniversary?p=882099#post882099\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've made my beef with Charnel Houses known elsewhere.</div> </div> </div> </div>Could i ask you in what thread you did that? I have only read praises to that supplement and i would like to read another point of view.<br /> <br /> <br /> As for the main question.<br /> I dont think Black Dog need to exist anymore 90% of what they put out its already covered in 20th.<ul><li>Formori: Freak legion. W20 and Wyrm book.</li> <li>Clanbook tzimice &amp; Baali. Lore of the clan plus all the other material on clans/bloodlines already there on V20th.</li> <li>Dirty Secret of the black hand is already out.</li> <li>Destiny price and ascension right hand dont need 20th counter parts better put their 20th counter parts into another compilation of gear, merit and rules. The sorcerer are also a nono because M20th developer decision of cut them off from 20th.</li> <li>Dead magic I maybe. Though i dont know how many rules need update in those.</li> <li>Hunter the reckoning: Wayward cant happen until we get a Hunter 20th, if ever but if they have release single faction book yet i doubt hunter is the game they would.</li> <li>And i guess the Wraith books. Dont know how many rules soah has.</li> </ul>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2179,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2179-lokiravenspeak","user":"LokiRavenSpeak","date":".  Phone mangled my post 07-03-2016, 10:29 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2179-lokiravenspeak","name":"LokiRavenSpeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-12T21:22:31-07:00","id":930704,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Coridan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/881500-will-black-dog-publishing-s-return-on-the-20-years-anniversary?p=882782#post882782\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The opening fiction of Clanbooks Baali was child rape. It was a good book (as was that opening story but I can understand the Black Dog label for it.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I've recently read this. It was not child rape. It was a child like vampire injecting bugs into a priests willy wonka","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3837-slimjimjohnson","name":"Slimjimjohnson","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"135"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-13T03:18:03-07:00","id":930755,"title":"","content":"I don't think it's needed anymore. As early as Demon: The Fallen there were books with full-on boobs on display (The Earthbound), and I reckon that stuff like the Slashers from Hunter: The Vigil would've been Black Dog back in the day but not so anymore.<br /> <br /> Speaking of, how are Slashers compared to Wayward Imbued?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12085-beriorn","name":"Beriorn","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12085_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-13T07:28:13-07:00","id":930834,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Beriorn</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/881500-will-black-dog-publishing-s-return-on-the-20-years-anniversary?p=930755#post930755\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Speaking of, how are Slashers compared to Wayward Imbued?</div> </div> </div> </div>Waywards, for all the innocents that MIGHT get caught in the line of fire, generally do some good, some of the time. Every mission for a Wayward doesn't end in complete disaster with dead innocent people, but the potential is always there.<br /> <br /> Slashers don't do any good, <b>as far as I know</b>. They're evil, plain and simple. <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">&quot;Steel isn't strong, boy. Flesh is stronger.&quot;</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/95-fat-larry","name":"Fat Larry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar95_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1337"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-13T14:46:53-07:00","id":931030,"title":"","content":"They're pretty different.<br /> <br /> Waywards are fanatics and extremists. The philosophies they take to such extremes have at least some grounding in &quot;good&quot; ethics, so as Larry pointed out, this means that they do good even if it rarely stays that simple.<br /> <br /> Slashers are killers. Anything beyond that is up to the individual. A Slasher can do good by deciding they like hunting murderers as the most exciting game, but any good they might do by killing bad people is incidental to their motivations. Hannibal Lecter is a pretty stereotypical example of a Slasher in media. His MO is to kill people that he considers &quot;bad&quot; for society, but that's not like the fanaticism of a Wayward killing monsters without worrying about collateral damage. He kills &quot;rude&quot; people that annoy him as a thin justification for the pleasure of killing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}